    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107-a1">

                <pb facs="0253" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg157"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 146 <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >bis.</hi>—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williamson to the captain commanding any of the
                        Pacific mail-steamers off or near the port of San José de Guatemala, or to
                        the commanders of any American vessels at or near said port.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1874-04-25T08:30:00-06:36"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April</hi> 25, 1874—8½
                    a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The President of Guatemala wishes yon to deliver on shore the person of Don José
                    Maria Gonzalez, who has committed a grave outrage upon the persons of American
                    citizens and British subjects. I second his wish, and request you to do so at
                    once.</p>
                <p>No one can claim an asylum from our country who has violated the laws of
                    civilized life to the extent Mr. Gonzalez has done.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. WILLIAMSON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
